Joint limits as box constraints in the IK (see UPSTREAM.md).

InverseKinematics solves with LBFGSpp's L-BFGS-B (LBFGSBSolver) instead of
L-BFGS, with per-joint bounds set by InverseKinematics::set_joint_limits /
JointData::set_joint_limits (unbounded by default, as before). The start is
projected onto the bounds. Also initializes niter, which was returned
uninitialized when the solver threw.

diff -ru a/include/fast_forward_kinematics/fast_inverse_kinematics.hpp b/include/fast_forward_kinematics/fast_inverse_kinematics.hpp
--- a/include/fast_forward_kinematics/fast_inverse_kinematics.hpp
+++ b/include/fast_forward_kinematics/fast_inverse_kinematics.hpp
@@ -3,11 +3,13 @@
